  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 201 PM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nMid-level high pressure continues to be the dominant feature through \nthe forecast period, with warm and mostly rain-free conditions \nexpected. Seabreeze convection will be possible in the afternoons, \nwith the best chances Saturday and Sunday as deep moisture (PWAT \nvalues ~2.1\" along the coast) interacts with an area of vorticity \nriding around the periphery of the ridge. \n\nTemperatures will remain hot, with highs in the 90s along the coast \nto around 105 over the Brush Country. The good news is that there \nwill be a bit more cloud cover this weekend, keeping the heat index \ngenerally below 110, though isolated locations could see heat index \nvalues up to 112. By early next week, expect heat advisory \nconditions to return.",
